00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.960
created inside of your Printify

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:14.960
dashboard, but if you come to your

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:16.240
products tab in your Shopify admin,

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:18.360
you'll be able to see all of the

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.720
products you created in here as well.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.240
Plus, if you come and open up your

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:23.120
settings and check out your shipping

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:25.200
profiles, you'll see that Printify has

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:27.080
also, now that it's been connected,

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:29.240
added in its own shipping rates for you,

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:31.720
too, which is great as it means we don't

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:33.560
have to do this ourselves. However, it's

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:35.800
up to you to choose which countries you

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:37.880
want to sell and ship to. You don't have

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:39.720
to ship everywhere in the world if you

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.920
don't want to, and you can choose that

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:44.160
by in the left side menu selecting

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:45.840
markets. Now, by default, you'll see

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:48.080
that it's usually set up so customers

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:50.280
based in the country that you live in

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:52.120
can already buy from you. So, for me, it

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:54.400
was set up by default to allow people

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:56.960
living here in New Zealand to be able to

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:58.640
buy from my store. But, if I'd like to

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:00.640
sell to more countries, that's easy. I

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:02.800
can just click to create a new market

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:04.920
and in this add all of the countries

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:07.000
that I'd like to ship to. You can add

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:09.040
all of them by ticking them all, or you

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:11.160
can go through and pick specific ones.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:12.880
It's entirely up to you. So, for

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:15.000
example, if you don't live in the

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:16.440
European Union and you speak English as

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.160
your primary language and will be

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:21.800
posting t-shirt videos in English, then

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:23.600
you might choose not to sell to the EU

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:25.680
since you're unlikely to get many

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:28.120
non-English customers from the EU

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:30.240
anyway. And for better or for worse, the

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:32.200
EU does have a bunch of complicated

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:34.160
rules and restrictions for international

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:36.520
sellers. And so, you might instead just

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:38.280
choose to ship only to Anglo countries

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:40.480
where the vast majority of your

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:42.240
customers will be coming from anyway,

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.840
which also conveniently happens to be

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:46.080
the countries that have less laws and

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:48.760
restrictions for international sellers,

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:51.160
such as the USA, Canada, Australia, New

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:52.560
Zealand, and the UK. But yes, either

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.560
way, once you've picked all of the

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:56.320
countries you'd like to sell to, you can

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:58.040
then just click save. And so, now we can

00:21:56.320 --> 00:22:00.160
continue setting up the store with the

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.840
Shopify sidekick. Tell it that you have

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:03.680
confirmed the t-shirts and shipping have

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:05.680
all been added in, and then ask it to

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:07.960
carry on with the setup. And so, as you

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:09.920
can see, next up, it recommended I set

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:11.880
up a payment processor. And luckily,

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:14.000
this is also pretty easy to do because

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:16.200
Shopify has their own built-in one that

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:18.040
you can use called Shopify Payments.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:20.360
However, to use it, they need to check

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:22.480
that you are a real person and confirm

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:23.920
your identity and to make sure that

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:25.880
you're not a scammer. And that was

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:28.200
simple to do. I just clicked the button

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:29.480
to open up Shopify Payment Settings,

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:31.880
then I clicked to start the setup

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:33.520
process. Now, for most people watching,

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:35.600
you probably don't have a registered

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:38.080
business, and so, if you don't, you can

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:39.120
just click to sell as an individual, and

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:41.120
then you'll need to fill out some

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:43.120
information and of course, provide proof

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:45.640
of identity and proof of address to

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:48.600
Shopify. Now, since this information

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:50.880
about where I live is private, I chose

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:53.400
not to film myself while I was filling

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:55.440
this information out. But once you are

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:58.440
indeed done, it will let you know that

00:22:55.440 --> 00:23:00.600
you are ready to accept payments, but

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:02.320
that you're not yet ready to get paid

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:04.360
since you haven't yet added in a bank

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:06.520
account number for Shopify to be able to

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:08.560
send your money to. So, all you've got

00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:11.360
to do is go in and add your bank account

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:12.400
number in, and once you do that, now

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:14.160
you'll see that it will switch to

00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:17.880
telling you that you can both accept

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:19.520
payments and receive payments. Nice. So,

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:21.680
then, after this, I just came back to

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:23.480
the Shopify AI Sidekick, and I told it

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:25.280
to move on to the next step. And as you

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:27.600
can see, it now recommended that I add

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:29.680
an install policy pages, such as terms

00:23:27.600 --> 00:23:31.600
of service, things like that. So, I

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:33.040
opened up the link that it gave me, and

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:35.240
there are two ways that you can write

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:37.200
these. One way is to open them up and

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:38.960
check to see if there are any pre-built

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:41.040
templates that Shopify has already

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:43.560
created for you. You can then just check

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:45.920
over this and fill in any extra details

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:47.600
that it asks for, like the information

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:49.520
here at the bottom of the terms of

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:51.680
service template that it just wants me

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:54.040
to fill in. Or you can come to any AI

00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:56.560
chatbot that you like, such as ChatGPT,

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:58.680
Gemini, or Claude, any of them will do,

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:00.560
and ask it to help you write a template.

00:23:58.680 --> 00:24:02.880
So, you can see I asked Claude here to

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:04.680
research Printify shipping information

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:06.880
and use it to write a shipping page

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:09.480
template for me, which it did, no

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:11.520
problem. That is. Either way, once I'd

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:13.280
finished that, I came back to Sidekick

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:15.360
and said I wanted it to move on to the

00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:17.320
next step. And this time, it suggested

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:19.240
that I now update the look of my store's

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:21.480
homepage. So, I clicked the button to

00:24:19.240 --> 00:24:23.640
open up the theme editor, and then I

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:25.560
clicked to edit my theme homepage. And

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:27.560
as you can see, our simple store is

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:29.760
actually pretty much set up to go as is

00:24:27.560 --> 00:24:31.760
design-wise. We just want to make two

00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:33.400
design tweaks to it. We're going to add

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:35.320
in a homepage banner, plus we're going

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:37.080
to add in a store logo, too. And

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:39.160
creating a logo with AI was pretty

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:41.200
simple. Here's how I did it. First, I

00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:43.120
just used AI to help me brainstorm a

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:45.040
name for my store. Then I came back to

00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:47.120
the Nano Banana image generator inside

00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:49.600
of Hexfield. I asked it to make me a

00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:51.440
simple landscape logo using my new store

00:24:49.600 --> 00:24:53.280
name. And out of the different options

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:55.160
that I got it to make for me, this one

00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:57.360
was my favorite, but I wanted to tweak

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:59.440
it a bit. So, I set it as a reference

00:24:57.360 --> 00:25:01.760
asked it to make the text black and the

00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:04.000
icon black and white. And check it out,

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:05.600
it made these changes for me, easy. So,

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:07.680
I downloaded it, then I came back to

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:10.080
Canva and just like in step two, I

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:12.400
uploaded my logo image and opened it up

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:13.920
to edit it. And I used the AI background

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:16.000
remover to make the background

00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:18.320
transparent. And then I resized the

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:21.080
image canvas and I dragged the image in

00:25:18.320 --> 00:25:23.480
the corners to resize the logo to fill

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.760
the entire canvas. And I just downloaded

00:25:23.480 --> 00:25:27.520
my logo as a PNG file with a transparent

00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:30.200
background. And then I came back to

00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:32.880
Shopify and I selected to add a new logo

00:25:30.200 --> 00:25:35.120
and I clicked to upload a new logo. And

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:37.200
of course, I uploaded the edited image

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:38.800
that I had just made with Canva. And

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:41.920
then that was it, my store now had a

00:25:38.800 --> 00:25:43.600
logo. Nice. So, next up, we're going to

00:25:41.920 --> 00:25:45.880
create our store homepage banner and

00:25:43.600 --> 00:25:47.960
again, this is pretty easy to do. It was

00:25:45.880 --> 00:25:49.880
just a quick two-step process. First, I

00:25:47.960 --> 00:25:51.440
picked one of my t-shirt designs and

00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:53.480
then I came back to the name banana

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:56.080
inside of Hexfield and I asked it to

00:25:53.480 --> 00:25:58.040
make a store banner image of a woman

00:25:56.080 --> 00:26:00.360
wearing my t-shirt and I uploaded the

00:25:58.040 --> 00:26:02.040
t-shirt picture as a reference image.

00:26:00.360 --> 00:26:03.640
And out of the different banner images

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:06.360
that it made for me, this one was my

00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:08.080
favorite. So, I downloaded it. Then back

00:26:06.360 --> 00:26:10.160
in my store theme editor, I clicked on

00:26:08.080 --> 00:26:12.480
the empty store banner and I selected to

00:26:10.160 --> 00:26:14.200
upload a new banner image. And then I

00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:16.360
uploaded this picture that I had just

00:26:14.200 --> 00:26:18.640
made with Hexfield. And as you can see,

00:26:16.360 --> 00:26:20.680
it looks great. Although, it had that

00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:23.120
big ugly text on it covering the

00:26:20.680 --> 00:26:25.160
picture. So, I just clicked that text

00:26:23.120 --> 00:26:26.960
and I deleted it. And then I just came

00:26:25.160 --> 00:26:28.800
to the store's welcome banner and hid it

00:26:26.960 --> 00:26:31.160
since it's not necessary and just

00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:33.520
clicked to save my new store design. And

00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:35.600
take a look, our starter store is ready.

00:26:33.520 --> 00:26:38.560
It is a nice clean design that looks

00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:40.560
great on both a computer, but also on a

00:26:38.560 --> 00:26:42.440
mobile device, too. If you want to make

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:44.760
any extra tweaks to your design, you can

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:46.880
totally go do so now. It is up to you,

00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:49.760
it's your store, so you can make any

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:51.360
design tweaks to it that you like. But,

00:26:49.760 --> 00:26:53.200
either way, now that we had our store

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:55.360
homepage finished, I came back to the

00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:57.520
Sidekick AI and asked it for the next

00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:59.440
step. And next up, it recommended that I

00:26:57.520 --> 00:27:01.320
double-check that Shopify sales tax

00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:03.080
feature was turned on. A lot of people

00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:05.240
don't know this, but Shopify has an

00:27:03.080 --> 00:27:07.440
inbuilt sales tax feature, which is very

00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:09.200
convenient. Then after that, I asked to

00:27:07.440 --> 00:27:11.120
move on to the next step. Sidekick

00:27:09.200 --> 00:27:12.520
recommended that I do an optional test

00:27:11.120 --> 00:27:14.880
purchase to make sure the store is

00:27:12.520 --> 00:27:16.520
working, which is super easy to do. You

00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:18.680
just click the option in your settings

00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:20.920
to turn the test purchase mode on, and

00:27:18.680 --> 00:27:23.040
then you can open up your store and add

00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:25.040
a product into your shopping cart and go

00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:27.280
through and just pretend to be a real

00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:29.560
customer actually buying it, and then

00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:31.760
use the pretend test credit card number

00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:33.600
as the payment method. And if the order

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:35.600
successfully goes through and shows up

00:27:33.600 --> 00:27:37.840
in your Shopify dashboard as a test

00:27:35.600 --> 00:27:40.840
order, like mine did, then you know that

00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:43.000
your checkout is working. Yay. So, after

00:27:40.840 --> 00:27:45.040
successfully testing my checkout, I

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.840
turned the test purchase mode off. And

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:48.720
then I asked Sidekick for the next step

00:27:46.840 --> 00:27:51.200
in the setup process, and it actually

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:53.560
recommended removing my store password

00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:55.800
and sending my store live. Although I

00:27:53.560 --> 00:27:58.800
did ask it, "Hey, should I maybe give my

00:27:55.800 --> 00:28:01.640
store a domain name first?" I think that

00:27:58.800 --> 00:28:03.560
the AI was going to get me to make one

00:28:01.640 --> 00:28:06.040
after I sent the store live, but I

00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:08.280
decided that I wanted to do it first

00:28:06.040 --> 00:28:10.560
before I made my store public. Either

00:28:08.280 --> 00:28:11.960
way, it was simple enough to add it in.

00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:14.000
You can see that all you need to do is

00:28:11.960 --> 00:28:15.920
tell Sidekick what domain name that you

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:18.080
want, and it will check to see if it is

00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:20.040
available. And if it is available, it'll

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:22.000
give you a link to where you can go and

00:28:20.040 --> 00:28:24.040
buy it. And it's pretty cool because

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:26.960
yes, while my domain name did

00:28:24.040 --> 00:28:28.840
technically cost me $9 to buy, Shopify,

00:28:26.960 --> 00:28:30.720
as part of the current promotion, are

00:28:28.840 --> 00:28:33.680
giving all new users who purchase a

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:35.880
domain a $20 credit rebate, which

00:28:33.680 --> 00:28:37.920
basically made it free for me, which I

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:40.480
love because who doesn't love free

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:42.400
stuff, right? Shopify also took care of

00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:44.320
the technical process of connecting my

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:46.000
domain name to my store for me. The

00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:48.480
technical name for this process is

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:50.480
called propagation, and propagation can

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:52.600
take some time. For me, it took about an

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:54.480
hour, but once the propagation process

00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:56.200
was over, it automatically switched to

00:28:54.480 --> 00:28:59.000
showing me that the domain was now

00:28:56.200 --> 00:29:00.960
connected. Nice. And with that, I was

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:02.880
pretty much done. It was time to move on

00:29:00.960 --> 00:29:05.040
to the next step, sending my store live

00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:06.800
and making it public. Because you see,

00:29:05.040 --> 00:29:08.720
by default, while you're still building

00:29:06.800 --> 00:29:10.880
your store and it's not yet ready for

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:13.280
the general public to access, Shopify

00:29:10.880 --> 00:29:15.120
hides it by placing this password screen

00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:17.640
on it so that people who try to go to

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:19.840
your store will get stuck behind this

00:29:17.640 --> 00:29:21.240
password screen, which is great. Don't

00:29:19.840 --> 00:29:23.040
get me wrong, while you're still

00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:25.280
building it and it's not yet ready for

00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:27.080
customers, but it's not so great once

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:29.200
your store is ready to start selling,

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:31.000
you know? So, just tell Sidekick that

00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:32.200
you're ready to send your store live and

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:33.960
it will take you to the preference

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:36.040
setting where the password privacy

00:29:33.960 --> 00:29:38.480
screen is turned on. You can then turn

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:40.400
the screen off and then just click save.

00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:43.080
And that's it. Your store is now live

00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:45.160
and public. Yay! We now have a simple,

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:47.200
clean print on demand t-shirt store that

00:29:45.160 --> 00:29:48.825
we can share on places like Instagram so

00:29:47.200 --> 00:29:50.520
that people can come and buy t-shirts

00:29:48.825 --> 00:29:53.400
[clears throat] from you that you show

00:29:50.520 --> 00:29:55.040
off in your viral videos. And obviously,

00:29:53.400 --> 00:29:56.960
you're welcome to make any additional

00:29:55.040 --> 00:29:58.880
tweaks to your design layout and store

00:29:56.960 --> 00:30:01.080
settings that you like before you do

00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:03.240
that. You can customize your store as

00:30:01.080 --> 00:30:05.280
much as you want. And if you'd like even

00:30:03.240 --> 00:30:07.000
more help in doing that, I actually have

00:30:05.280 --> 00:30:08.840
an advanced Shopify print on demand

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:10.760
tutorial video here that you can watch

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:12.880
and follow along with for even more

00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:14.520
design and setup tips. So, if you're

